    <summary>Before you start</summary>
    <div class="inner">
      <ul>
        <li><b>Same candidate for everyone.</b> Build the Roam extension and the Obsidian plugin from <code>b3796a70</code>. Results only count for the commit they tested.</li>
        <li><b>Spaces.</b> At least two Roam graphs and two Obsidian vaults, one more space for the three-space cases, and one space outside the test group for access checks. Use two groups: G1 for everyone and G2 for a subset.</li>
        <li><b>Accounts.</b> Everyone in a Roam graph uses that graph's database account, and each vault has its own. Group membership belongs to a graph or vault, not to a person.</li>
        <li><b>Roam settings.</b> Turn on Node sharing and the Suggestive mode overlay (import needs it until ENG-2297), and keep stored relations on (the pending-relations list needs them). Reload after any change. Suggestive mode also changes what syncs, so note which mode each result used.</li>
        <li><b>Obsidian settings.</b> In the plugin settings press Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+A to open the Admin panel, turn on “(BETA) Sync mode enable”, then reload. For Source cases, the vault needs a node type named “Source” and an accepted relation type from Evidence to Source.</li>
        <li><b>Timing.</b> Roam syncs about every 5 minutes, at least 130 s apart across clients; reloading the graph syncs right away. Obsidian syncs 5 s after the last edit, and fully on load and on publish. Destinations only change when you press Refresh.</li>
        <li><b>Isolated cases</b> break or delete data on purpose. Run them on throwaway spaces and a throwaway group, never on a graph people use.</li>
        <li><b>Access-control cases</b> (SEC) run only against a local database, by an engineer. File confirmed ones as private Linear tickets, not public GitHub issues.</li>
      </ul>
